\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Site symmetries commute with restriction}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Let corresponding transformations act by coordinate maps #{b,b'} and the same constant linear or conjugate-linear value map #{L} on a pair of grids. If #{b'\iota=\iota b}, the transformations commute with \vocabk{restriction}{fdip-01BP}. This applies to period-preserving signed coordinate permutations, site-centered reflections, charge conjugation with the same value structures, the site-centered spinor time map of \ref{fdip-0184} and the \vocabk{graded total inversion}{fdip-019C}.}

\proof{\p{Both evaluations at #{x} give #{L\psi'(k b x)}. The coordinate maps in the listed transformations are signed permutations, or the identity, and the hypotheses keep their implementing value maps fixed. For the one-step link-plane reflection #{t\mapsto 1-t} the two site images are #{1-kt} and #{k(1-t)}. Their difference has absolute value #{k-1}, strictly between zero and #{kN} for #{k>1}. This reflection therefore fails the coordinate condition.}}
